L2 evict_first cache policy on the routed-expert weight copies of the split-materialized W4A8
phase kernels (W4A8MaterializedPhase1Kernel FC1 / W4A8MaterializedPhase2Kernel FC2), requested per
launch with fused_moe._impl.evict_first_weights() (adapter/moe_b12x_next.py, DSV41_MOE_EVICT_FIRST,
decode-sized CUDA-graph captures only). New intrinsic cp_async4_shared_global_l2hint
(cp.async.cg.shared.global.L2::cache_hint [smem], [gmem], 16, policy) with the policy from the
existing create_l2_evict_first_policy (createpolicy.fractional.L2::evict_first.b64 policy, 1.0),
created once per thread at kernel entry. A compile-time flag on both phase kernels; the dynamic
kernel cache key gains ("evict_first_weights",) only when on, so the stock kernels and their keys
are unchanged and both coexist in one process. Weight scale words (SFB), activations, the
intermediate and outputs keep the default policy.
Idea: Christopher Owen, spark-ds41f #966 (Apache-2.0), there on TileLang TMA weight loads; this is
a port to the b12x CuTe kernels. Applies after scale-codes; the coded phase kernels share the same weight
copies (their scale staging is unchanged). Apache License 2.0 (runtime/b12x_next/LICENSE).

